<title>POLAND: Polish Dec broad money up 5.1 pct, up 29.0 in '96.</title>
<headline>Polish Dec broad money up 5.1 pct, up 29.0 in '96.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 6.57 billion zlotys, or 5.1 percent, in December to 134.49 billion after a 1.4 pct rise in November, preliminary central bank figures showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Broad money supply grew 29.0 percent in 1996 period against 31.5 percent in the same period of last year.  </p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		     DEC     NOV    DEC 1995</p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)	    5.1     1.4	2.1</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		 134.49  127.91   104.25</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)    23.36   22.87    21.30</p>
<p>  National currency		   111.12  105.04    82.95</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		  23.56   23.67    19.53</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector  80.24   76.95    56.21</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
